# Everything `regenerate.sh` produces.
#
# The three `.ct` directories and `session.toml` are NOT committed. They
# used to be, on the reasoning that re-recording on every CI run would
# make the suite depend on a browser and a Rust toolchain — which is
# true, and is the price of the tests meaning anything. A recording made
# by the current recorder and replayed by the current replayer proves the
# two agree with each other and goes on proving it after the recorder
# changes; committing it turns a cross-tier integration test into a cache
# with an assertion attached. `scripts/materialize-recording.sh` records
# once per build into the gitignored `target/test-recordings/`, keyed on
# the demo's sources and on the *content* of every recorder binary, so a
# recorder change re-records instead of going unnoticed.
#
# These entries are what a hand-run `regenerate.sh` leaves beside the
# sources when no output directory is given.
frontend.ct/
frontend-wasm.ct/
backend.ct/
session.toml
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/package-lock.json
frontend/balance_calc.wasm
frontend/balance_calc.wasm.manifest.json
wasm-src/target/

# Dropped into the directory by the nix dev shell's git hooks.
.pre-commit-config.yaml
